## Post-Migration Update Guide
 
When the migrated application is ready:
 
### 1. Update the base URL
 
```powershell
$env:E2E_BASE_URL = "http://your-new-app-url"
```
 
### 2. Update URL routes (if changed)
 
Edit `Config/Routes.cs` — update the string values to the new Razor Pages routes.
 
### 3. Update changed selector labels (if any)
 
If the new UI uses different label text or button text for any element:
 
1. Update the value in `docs/e2e-baseline/selector-registry/{PageName}.selectors.json`
2. Re-run: `@e2e-baseline-test-generator {PageName}` in Copilot Agent Mode
   to regenerate `Selectors/{PageName}Selectors.cs`
3. `Pages/{PageName}Page.cs` and `Specs/{PageName}Tests.cs` remain unchanged
 
### 4. Replace Telerik control interactions
 
For any Telerik control that now has a native HTML equivalent in the new UI:
 
In `Pages/{PageName}Page.cs`, replace the `TelerikHelper.*` call in the
relevant method with a semantic Playwright locator call. The method signature
and the spec file do not change.
 
Example — before (pre-migration):
```csharp
public async Task FillDateOfBirth(DateTime date) =>
    await TelerikHelper.FillDatePicker(page, Selectors.Fields.DateOfBirth, date);
```
 
After (post-migration with native date input):
```csharp
public async Task FillDateOfBirth(DateTime date) =>
    await page.GetByLabel("Date of Birth").FillAsync(date.ToString("yyyy-MM-dd"));
```
 
### 5. Run the tests
 
```powershell
dotnet test
```
 
All green = functional equivalence proven.
 
